From 7fe1a2e99e579530d1bd306e74bd7f3c428a49f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: danilo neves cruz <cruzdanilo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:18:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: aim web taps again when they land on another element

a page can still move after the settle confirms it quiet, without
touching the dom: a component that measures its layout on a timer
resizes a sheet a few frames later. the tap then presses at the old
point, on whatever is there now, like the sheet's backdrop.

the first press after a settle is guarded: the web driver rejects it
when the page moved since the settle, and otherwise records the element
at the tap point and swallows the press if it lands on another one.
either way the tap command settles again and resolves its selector
anew, until the press lands or the settle timeout passes.
